\section{Experiments}

\subsection{Data Source and Preprocessing}

A-share full-market stocks from January 2015 to December 2024 are selected as research samples, excluding ST, *ST stocks, and newly listed stocks with less than 6 months of trading history. Factor data includes technical indicators (momentum, volatility, RSI) and liquidity factors (volume, turnover). All factors undergo market capitalization neutralization and industry neutralization, with a 3:1 split for training and test sets.

\subsection{Comparison Models and Evaluation Metrics}

We compare the following methods:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Equal-Weight Multi-Factor}: Traditional multi-factor model with equal factor weights;
    \item \textbf{XGBoost Classification}: Binary classification (up/down) with XGBoost;
    \item \textbf{Single Ranking Model}: Single LightGBM with standard ranking loss;
    \item \textbf{RRF Fusion (Ours)}: Proposed method with return-Sharpe aware loss and RRF fusion.
\end{itemize}

Evaluation metrics include annualized return, maximum drawdown, Sharpe ratio, and information ratio.

